# App Review demo account for scripts/review_account.sh (skill heji-review-account, DECISIONS #71).
# Sourced as bash. The password is never here: it lives in ~/Credentials/review-accounts.env and
# App Store Connect. After the first setup, give the account its example trip once:
#   WAYPACK_URL=https://waypack.hejitech.workers.dev node projects/waypack/services/mcp/scripts/seed-dev.mjs \
#     appreview+waypack@hejitech.com --review "<password>"

REVIEW_EMAIL="appreview+waypack@hejitech.com"
# The Worker that serves POST /api/review-sign-in, and where it runs.
WORKER_DIR="projects/waypack/services/mcp"
WRANGLER_ENV="production"
SITE="https://waypack.hejitech.workers.dev"
BUNDLE_ID="com.hejitech.waypack"

# App Store Connect › App Review Information › Notes.
REVIEW_NOTES="Sign in: on the first screen tap \"Sign in with email\" (below Continue with Google) and use the demo account above. People create accounts with Sign in with Apple or Google; email sign-in is only for accounts we hand out, such as this one.

The account already has a trip: \"Sequoia Winter Weekend\", planned by an AI agent and published to Waypack. Tap it to open the trip, which downloads with its offline map (this account has Waypack Pro, so the offline map is included). Then try Today, the map and the Assistant in airplane mode: everything works without a connection.

Trips are made by the person's own AI agent (Claude, ChatGPT and others) through Waypack's MCP server; the app is a free viewer with no purchases. Pro is sold on the web only and the app doesn't link to it."
